tial sequel  called hellraiser 5 hellfire  a different sequel involving a matchup  between pinhead and michael myers was  also considered  neither prospect has come to pass  hellfire didn't take off because the  screenplay was too big and too expensive  with the film culminating in a massive  puzzle box sealing around all of london  and attempting to bring the hell god  leviathan to earth  demand for a new hellraiser simply  wasn't big enough to get hollywood on  board  creative clive barker was booted off the  project subsequent sequels were released  only on home video and the actual fifth  hellraiser movie inferno was a strange  psychological murder mystery with barely  any pinhead  welcome to hell bubba hotep was written  and directed by don coscarelli who also  created the legendary phantasm series  and the sword and sorcery classic the  beastmaster  bubba hotep being a horror comedy is  quite a bit different from those films  but very much beloved in its own right  fans have been clamoring for a sequel  for years and they came close to getting  one  the title was going to be bubba  nosferatu cursed of the she vampires  yet it didn't come to pass because bruce  campbell simply didn't want to reprise  his role  as campbell told entertainment weekly i  killed it i killed it for me  i told the creators that i didn't want  to dance around it anymore i feel that  the first one was a nice little gem and  you don't have to make a sequel for  everything  go make it you know get somebody else i  don't want to do it so that one i'm just  going to let go  campbell did drop an interesting  bombshell in that interview ron perlman  apparently almost took over the role  most fans would agree he would indeed  make a fine replacement  amazingly paul giamatti has also been  attached to this possible sequel but  that sort of talent on board she  vampires could more than live up to its  predecessor  with so many classic horror films being  remade and rebooted it's hard for a fan  